{
  "schema": "loom.runtime_profile/1",
  "domain": "actions",
  "revision": 1,
  "description": "Catalogue of actions: ONE kind of entity. An action is atomic (implemented by code or an adapter: use_model, save, share) or composite (steps of other actions, defined here as data). Both have the same shape: declared typed inputs and outputs, effect flags and a status, plus what the matching engine (loom/include/loom/action_rules.h) needs: `requires` (traits the input element must have; a class id is a trait of its own), `produces` (traits of the output element), the two axes of GRAF_HUB_KOD_SILNIK §6 (`content_op`: what the action does to the content, `form_op`: whether it reads a form into content or expresses content in a form) and the declared `cost` (relative: 1 = one ordinary model call, not money) and `confidence` (0..1) used to rank chains. A new action fits every existing class whose traits meet its `requires` without editing the class. Which of the fitting actions are default, need confirmation or are denied is decided by the rules (data/runtime/action_rules.pack). A call to use_model may name its action; an unknown, planned or non-model action is refused before any send. Entries with port/action are reachable through loom_invoke(port, action, json); their params carry field descriptions (has_default/default/edit) and http the server route. All numbers and ops are calibration, editable in the overlay.",
  "defaults": {
    "schema": "loom.action_catalogue/1",
